<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William MacGregor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1846">1846</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William MacGregor was a Scottish physician and colonial governor. As administrator of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a> from 1888 to 1898 he explored the interior, set up government stations, appointed village constables and restricted land sales to Europeans, foundations later taken over by Australian Papua; he went on to govern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lagos">Lagos</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> and Queensland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-macgregor.jpg" alt="William MacGregor" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_William_MacGregor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
